ifT -- SEQ 472 (Tony, 2026-10-30): IF on the new road, PRE-REGISTERED ON TRUNK before the build.

This file is not run alone. pop.sh builds two inputs per row, one process each under an alarm: everything above this file's
`stop();`, then the row on the OLD road (the statement itself) or on the NEW road (the rule called by name, then testOP on
what it handed back, except IF-0, which builds and does not run), then `IF NEXT` and a sentinel. Read by value, with the
old road's print as the control.

TODAY (2026-10-30, measured): If has no action, and it is `defer`, so its STATEMENt child is PRINt's label with PRINt's
action parked on it (deferredAbove), not an instruct. testOP on the If label takes its first child, the EXPRESSIOn label, as
the op and calls a null operat: IF-1, IF-2 and IF-3 die with exit 139. IF-4's STARt seq skips the If (not an instruct) and
prints 1 3.

ROWS -- id | old-road statement | new-road statement (testOP follows it, except IF-0)
IF-0||it1 = If("if qa < qb; print 77:;");
IF-1|if qa < qb; print 77:;|it1 = If("if qa < qb; print 77:;");
IF-2|if qa > qb; print 77:;|it1 = If("if qa > qb; print 77:;");
